{
 "version": 1,
 "_about": "(polish1 D2) How each reworked enemy moves (game/enemy_rig.gd). An enemy uses the style named by its data 'moves' (else its 'model'). Angles in degrees on the model's pivots (Hips, Spine, Head, Jaw, ArmL / ForeL, ArmR / ForeR, LegL / ShinL, LegR / ShinR, or any other node a style names). Signs: x+ swings a hanging limb FORWARD (an arm raised in front, a leg stepping out) and tips the Spine / Head BACK; a knee bends with Shin x-; the left arm goes OUT with z-, the right with z+. gait: full_at = m/s at which the walk is at full size, cadence = steps against the usual stride (1 = normal), leg / knee / arm / elbow = swing sizes, arm_out = arms held away from the sides, arms_up = arms raised in front (the drowned reach), bob = metres the hips rise each step, sway / twist = the torso's roll / turn with the stride, lean = forward lean at full speed, crouch = bent knees and hips all the time, limp = 0..1 a dragged right leg, jerk = 0..1 a stepped rattling walk, head_loll = the head rolls about. idle: breath, look (turning the head while it stands), twitch 0..1 (sudden head jerks), jaw / jaw_rate (opening and closing). osc: extra swings [{node, axis, amp, phase (deg), rate (cycles a second; 0 = with the stride), with_speed, spin (true = keeps turning, `rate` turns a second)}]. wind = the pose at the top of a wind-up, strike = right after the blow, aim = held while it shoots, recoil = on a shot. death: slump (goes limp) or crumble (falls apart). variants = how many of the model's V1_ / V2_ / V3_ sets may be shown (0 = all).",
